"final_claim": {"task_id": "t_8c505e24", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1188, 906], "window": [0, 35570], "confidence": 0.83, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting 600-unit cascade from 1188 to 906 exists. The two nodes' activity is anti-phased: 906 is active early (45 events before t=5000, none after t~21000) while 1188 is active late (51 of 71 events after t=25000). 1188's out-neighbours and 906's in-neighbours are completely disjoint, so no 2-hop directed path exists even statically. The static k-hop 'connection' runs through 172 and 213, but those edges point INTO 1188 and do not occur at all before t=25000, whereas their links to 906 (via 1264/1181) are single early events. The static reachability is an artefact of both nodes being high-degree hubs in a large 6712-event graph, not evidence of temporal influence."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**Analysis summary:**\n\n1. **Temporal anti-phasing (decisive).** Node 1188's activity ramps up late: 0 events before t=5000, only ~20 events before t=25000, and 51 of its 71 events after t=25000 (step_06). Node 906's activity is the mirror image: 45 events in [0,5000], decaying to 1 event in [20001,25000] and **zero events after t\u224821000** (step_07, step_09). Any influence leaving 1188 would have to reach 906 while 906 was still active, i.e. before ~21000, when 1188 had barely acted.\n\n2. **No short directed route.** 1188's out-neighbourhood (68 nodes, step_04) and 906's in-neighbourhood (66 nodes, step_05) are **disjoint** \u2014 no 2-hop path 1188\u2192x\u2192906 exists at all, even ignoring time.\n\n3. **The apparent static connections are direction-reversed and mistimed.** The 2-hop structure (step_03, step_08/step_11) links the two via 172 and 213, but those are edges *into* 1188 ([172,1188], [213,1188]), and even so, 1188 has **no interaction with 172 or 213 anywhere in [0,25000]** (step_12, step_14), while the downstream legs 1264\u2192906 and 1181\u2192906 exist only as single early events (step_13, step_15). The ordering is backwards and the legs are separated by far more than the 600-unit relay limit.\n\n4. **Confounder controls.** High volume (6712 events, step_01) and high degree of both hubs (71 and 69 partners, step_02) explain why a static path can be found; the disjoint directed neighbourhoods and inverted activity timelines show this is popularity/aggregation artefact, not a cascade.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8c505e24\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1188, 906],\n  \"window\": [0, 35570],\n  \"confidence\": 0.83,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting 600-unit cascade from 1188 to 906 exists. The two nodes' activity is anti-phased: 906 is active early (45 events before t=5000, none after t~21000) while 1188 is active late (51 of 71 events after t=25000). 1188's out-neighbours and 906's in-neighbours are completely disjoint, so no 2-hop directed path exists even statically. The static k-hop 'connection' runs through 172 and 213, but those edges point INTO 1188 and do not occur at all before t=25000, whereas their links to 906 (via 1264/1181) are single early events. The static reachability is an artefact of both nodes being high-degree hubs in a large 6712-event graph, not evidence of temporal influence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 43518, "total_output_tokens": 8606, "total_tokens": 52124, "total_latency_ms": 116727, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}